  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a variational split-step quantum walk Adaptive Distribution Generator implemented in CUDA-Q GPU simulation. A 5-qubit setup (1 coin + 4 position qubits) is used to approximate a log-normal distribution for option pricing on a 16-point grid, producing call-price errors ranging from about 3.4% to 19.9% compared with Black–Scholes. Additional simulations show fitting of six 1D distributions and generation of 8×8 digit patterns using entangled quantum walkers.",
